In the triangle shown, James decides to write a number of pages, $x$, to one friend each week. The number of pages he writes must satisfy the triangle inequality with the other two sides being 5 pages and 6 pages. Additionally, if it’s a special week (like a holiday), he writes 2 more pages than usual. Given that there are 10 special weeks in a year, what is the positive difference between the greatest and least possible integral values of $x$ that he can write in a regular week, and how many pages does he write in a year? 

[asy]
defaultpen(linewidth(0.7));
pair a,b,c;
b = (1,2); c = (3,0);
draw(a--b--c--a);
label("$x$",a--b,dir(135)); label("5",b--c,dir(45)); label("6",c--a,S);
[/asy]

