A square with side length 2 is rotated about one vertex by an angle of $\alpha,$ where $0^\circ < \alpha < 90^\circ$ and $\cos \alpha = \frac{3}{5}.$  Find the area of the shaded region that is common to both squares. 

[asy]
unitsize(2 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, Bp, Cp, Dp, P;

A = (0,0);
B = (-2,0);
C = (-2,-2);
D = (0,-2);
Bp = rotate(aCos(3/5))*(B);
Cp = rotate(aCos(3/5))*(C);
Dp = rotate(aCos(3/5))*(D);
P = extension(C,D,Bp,Cp);

fill(A--Bp--P--D--cycle,gray(0.7));
draw(A--B---C--D--cycle);
draw(A--Bp--Cp--Dp--cycle);

label("$\alpha$", A + (-0.5,-0.15));
[/asy]

